# Security baseline

Baseline org standard for all services and frontends in this repository.

**VAPT addendum:** `docs/security/vapt-prevention-guardrails.md` · Team rules: `vapt-spring.mdc`, `vapt-webapp.mdc`, `vapt-pr-review.mdc`

---

## 1. Authentication

| Requirement | Standard |
|-------------|----------|
| Protocol | OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect (Okta) or JWT Bearer — no custom auth schemes |
| Session model | Stateless JWT for REST APIs; document if cookie sessions are used |
| MFA | Required for admin/backoffice portals |
| Logout | Invalidate server-side tokens, clear client state, revoke IdP session where SSO applies |
| Token blacklist | Fail-closed on infrastructure errors — never accept revoked tokens when Redis is unavailable |
| Dev bypass | Static dev tokens and `permit-all` **local only** — never in lab/SIT/UAT/prod |

**CSRF:** cookie sessions need CSRF tokens or SameSite + framework defaults; Bearer-only SPAs omit CSRF but must not put tokens in query strings.

---

## 2. Authorization

| Requirement | Standard |
|-------------|----------|
| Model | RBAC or ABAC; least privilege |
| Enforcement | **Server-side on every endpoint** — filter-level `authenticated()` alone is insufficient for admin APIs |
| Annotations | `@PreAuthorize` (or equivalent) on every controller method that mutates or exposes sensitive data |
| Client UI | Hiding nav links is **not** authorization — enforce in BFF, `+layout.server.ts`, or service layer |
| Trust boundary | Never trust client-supplied role/permission headers or query params |
| Bypass flags | No `MethodSecurityBypass`-style flags that disable authz in shared environments |

- **Authentication vs authorization:** verify caller identity (JWT, session, mTLS) at the edge; propagate principal to services. Enforce **RBAC/ABAC** and **resource-scoped** checks in the **service that owns the data** — not only at the gateway.
- **BOLA / IDOR:** for every `{id}` path, confirm the principal may access **that** instance (tenant/org/user scope); never trust client-supplied IDs without authorized lookup.

---

## 3. Secrets & Sensitive Data

| Requirement | Standard |
|-------------|----------|
| Storage | Environment variables or secret vaults — never in code, commits, rules, or logs |
| Client exposure | No backend URLs, API keys, RBAC matrices, or role names in client bundles |
| Env prefixes | `PUBLIC_*` / `VITE_*` only for intentionally public values — review before merge |
| PII in URLs | User IDs, tokens, and credentials in request **body or headers**, not query strings |
| Logging | Sanitize dynamic log values (`Encode.forJava()` in Java; equivalent elsewhere) |
| DB access | Least-privilege DB users per service; rotate keys per org policy |
| Responses | `@JsonIgnore` on sensitive response fields; no secrets in error bodies, logs, or client bundles |

---

## 4. Cookies & Client Storage

| Attribute | Session / auth cookies |
|-----------|------------------------|
| `HttpOnly` | **Required** |
| `Secure` | **Required** in production |
| `SameSite` | `Lax` or `Strict` |
| Auth tokens | Prefer HttpOnly cookies over `localStorage` / `sessionStorage` for session identifiers |
| Cache | Never cache user identity across logout without explicit invalidation |

---

## 5. File Uploads

| Check | Required |
|-------|----------|
| Server-side validation | **Always** — client `accept=` is supplemental only |
| Size limit | Explicit per endpoint |
| Content validation | Magic-byte / MIME sniffing + structure parse (e.g. CSV header row) |
| Extension allowlist | Supplemental — not sole check |
| Authorization | `@PreAuthorize` on all admin upload endpoints |
| Virus scan | Recommended for production (async queue) |

---

## 6. HTTP Security Headers

| Header | Value |
|--------|-------|
| `Strict-Transport-Security` | `max-age=31536000` (with HTTPS) |
| `X-Content-Type-Options` | `nosniff` |
| `X-Frame-Options` | `DENY` or `SAMEORIGIN` |
| `Content-Security-Policy` | Restrict script/style sources; no `'unsafe-inline'` unless justified |
| `Referrer-Policy` | `no-referrer` or `strict-origin-when-cross-origin` |

Remove fingerprinting headers (`X-Powered-By`, `Server` version leaks) where configurable.

**CORS:** explicit allowed origins in production; avoid `*` with credentials.

**CSP / XSS:** define CSP for apps rendering HTML; restrict script sources — see `frontend-web.mdc` for XSS discipline.

---

## 7. API Security

- Versioned paths (`/api/v1/...`)
- Authentication on all non-health endpoints
- Rate limiting at edge or BFF for auth, admin, and upload endpoints
- Input validation at API boundary (`@Valid`, Bean Validation)
- Parameterized queries / JPA named parameters only — no SQL string concatenation
- Appropriate HTTP status codes (401/403/405/406 — not 200 with error body)
- Do not leak stack traces, internal hostnames, or schema details in production errors

---

## 8. Production Hygiene

- `DEBUG` off in production
- No demo/debug routes (`/api/env-var`, `/api/echo`) in prod builds
- Source maps disabled in production client bundles unless explicitly approved
- `app.security.permit-all=false` in all deployed environments

---

## 9. Supply Chain

- Dependency scanning in CI (OWASP Dependency-Check, Snyk, Dependabot) — see `quality-and-testing.mdc`
- **SBOM** (CycloneDX/SPDX) when compliance requires; pin via lockfiles; document license policy if required

